# Deep Digger | Catch That Bug

When investigating stubborn, flaky, intermittent, or high-impact failures:
- Never confuse symptom with root cause.
- Maintain competing causal hypotheses.
- Use discriminating experiments before patching.
- Validate causal fixes via baseline reproduction, intervention, reversal, and negative control (A/B/A/C).

## CLI Quickstart
```bash
# Initialize case ledger
deep-digger init cases/incident-01 --title "Cache eviction failure" --symptom "Intermittent 500 error on logout"

# Add competing hypotheses
deep-digger hypothesis cases/incident-01 --claim "Race condition in cache eviction" --test "Concurrent logout stress test"
deep-digger hypothesis cases/incident-01 --claim "Stale DNS TTL resolution" --test "Mock DNS resolver verification"

# Generate evaluation report
deep-digger report cases/incident-01
```
